  "summary_en": "Letter from Toronto's Accessibility Advisory Committee to City Council responding to Ontario's proposed pilot for automated micro-utility (sidewalk delivery) devices. It recommends municipal by-law amendments banning their operation on sidewalks and cycle tracks and parking or storing them, with $150 fines, citing accessibility and Vision Zero.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Summarises MTO's proposed pilot: 125 kg, 74 cm width, 10 km/h sidewalk speed, operator oversight, insurance, municipal opt-in.",
   "Recommends defining 'micro-utility device' in Toronto Municipal Code Chapters 886 and 950.",
   "Proposes banning operation on sidewalks and cycle tracks, and parking, storing or leaving them on highways or sidewalks.",
   "Proposes $150 penalties for new offences.",
   "Argues the devices endanger people with disabilities, children and seniors, contrary to AODA obligations and Vision Zero."
  ],
